    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "so u basically think policy is the main culprit here. some people argue that these economic shifts are just inevitable parts of progress and that trying to fix them with more regulation or higher taxes just hurts growth. do u think those arguments have any merit, or are they just excuses for why the gap is widening?",
